  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## Setlist highlights\n\n- **A Good Woman's Love**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 13 archived performances [7]\n- **Down the Road**: rare: 9 archived performances [7]\n- **Walk on Boy**: back after 117 archived shows (438 days) [7]\n- **Road to Columbus**: back after 135 archived shows (517 days); rare: 3 archived performances [7]\n- **Banks of the Ohio**: rare: 3 archived performances [7]\n- **Here Comes the Sun**: rare: 10 archived performances [7]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **billystrings2019-11-19** (recommended): source not stated; 23 songs; 122 min; rated 4/5 by 2 [1]. Said about its sound: Static is audible on the louder passages, even though the recorder's meters never reached the red [3]\n- **billystrings2019-11-19.shure**: source not stated; 23 songs; 122 min; rated 2.5/5 by 2 [2]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- The sold-out crowd danced together, and the Beachland's old wooden floor bounced gently underfoot [4]\n- The reviewer says they were the audience member who shouted a request to help change a tire [4]\n- Crowd members seemed to shout for \"Away From The Mire\"; the band joked back, pretending to hear \"Light my fire?\" [5]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **billystrings2019-11-19**: taped by Scott Plumer; transferred by Scott Plumer; source: Beyerdynamic MCE86II > ART Phantom II > Marantz PMD660 [1]. Also: The taper ran a second complete rig at the same show, which sounds better than this one [3]\n- **billystrings2019-11-19.shure**: taped by Scott Plumer; transferred by Scott Plumer; source: Shure BG4.0 > Tascam Dr-05 [2]",
